hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2971","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Kathir, on the authority of Asim bin Laqit, on the authority of his father, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you perform ablution, continue to inhale as long as you are not fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2972","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Saeed, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of Omar, He said: I was anxious one day, so I kissed while I was fasting, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I did a great thing. I kissed while I was fasting. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What do you think if you rinse your mouth with water while you are fasting?” I said: There is no harm in that. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “So what?” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith and it is early and safe, and Abd al-Malik ibn Sa`id narrated it from him. One and we do not know who this is from"
"2973","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Hajjaj, Ibn Jurayj said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Abu Salih, that he heard Abu Hurairah, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the odor from the mouth of a fasting person will be sweeter to God on the Day of Resurrection than the fragrance of \Musk\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"2974","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace, to kiss me. I said: I am fasting. He said: I am fasting. So he kissed me. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2975","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to kiss while he was fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2976","Ali bin Hajar told me, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I said to Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim: I heard your father speaking, on the authority of Aisha, That the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to kiss her while he was fasting”? He was silent for an hour, then said: Yes"
"2977","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Musa bin Tariq reported, saying: I heard Musa bin Uqba, mentioning on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, that he asked Aisha, about the qiblah for the fasting person, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss while he was fasting,” then she laughed."
"2978","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed reported, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “And he used to kiss some of his wives while he was fasting.” The disagreement over Al-Zuhri was mentioned in this report."
"2979","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Usama bin Zaid told me, that Ibn Shihab told him, on the authority of Urwa, that Aisha told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “kiss while he was fasting.” Aisha said: Which of you was the one who To raise him from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? The disagreement over Aqeel bin Khalid in the hadith of Al-Zuhri"
"2980","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh reported, saying: In the book of my uncle, on the authority of Uqail, that Ibn Shihab informed him, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss while he was fasting.”"
"2981","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Aqeel told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, that she told him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissed her while he was fasting,” followed by Muammar."
"2982","Ismail bin Masoud reported, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Muammar told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissed her while he was fasting. “The disagreement over Ibn Abi Dhib"
"2983","Issa bin Ahmad Al-Asqalani Al-Balkhi and Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman reported, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, And Salih bin Abi Hassan, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss her while he was fasting.”"
"2984","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, he said: Ibn Abi Fudaik told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Harith Bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss her while he was He is fasting. There is a lot of disagreement over Yahya bin Abi. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2985","Mahmoud bin Khaled Al-Dimashqi told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Amr told us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Abu Salamah told me He said: Aisha told me, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to kiss her while he was fasting.” The disagreement over Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya, who is the son of Abi Kathir."
"2986","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam al-Tarsusi reported, saying: Ishaq, meaning Ibn Yusuf, told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawi, on the authority of Yahya, who is the son of Abu Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss her while he was fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2987","Amr bin Ali reported, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Yahya told me, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss her while he was fasting.”"
"2988","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Abu Salamah told us, on the authority of Urwa, that Aisha told him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss her while he was fasting.” The disagreement of Ali bin Al-Mubarak, And Shayban had a lot of respect for Yahya Ibn Abi. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2989","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, Harun bin Ismail Abu Al-Hasan said, he said: Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya told us Ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss her while he was fasting.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"2990","Muhammad bin Sahl bin Askar reported to Al-Bukhari, saying: Ubayd Allah told us, saying: Shaiban reported, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz told him, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to kiss while he was fasting.” Muawiyah bin Peace (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2991","Muhammad bin Yahya told me, he said: Muammar bin Yamar told us, he said: Muawiyah, who is Ibn Salam, told us, he said: Yahya told me, He said: Abu Salama told me, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz told him, that Urwa bin Al-Zubair told him, that Aisha told him, “ “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss her while he was fasting.” It was narrated by Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Zainab, on the authority of Umm Salamah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2992","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Salem bin Nuh told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abi Salamah, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: It was in the hadith that “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissed her.” And he is fasting,” Mukhtasar, Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is an error from the hadith of Qatadah, which mentioned the disagreement over Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj. In this hadith"
"2993","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam reported, saying: Ishaq reported, meaning Ibn Bakr bin Mudar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, she said: My mother told me, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “kiss while he was fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2994","Issa bin Hammad reported, he said: Al-Layth reported, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman. On the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissed him while he was fasting.”"
"2995","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissed And he said salaam while he was fasting. Abu Qays disagreed with them."
"2996","Yusuf bin Hammad Al-Ma’ani Al-Basri reported, saying: Sufyan bin Habib told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Qais, he said: Amr ibn al-Aas sent me to Umm Salamah to ask her: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kiss while he was fasting? And he said: If she says: No, then tell her that Aisha reported that “he used to kiss her while he was fasting.” So I asked her and she said: No, so I said: Aisha was told, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss her while he was fasting,” so she said: Perhaps he could not contain his love for her."
"2997","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Farukh, that Umm Salamah said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss me while he was fasting and I was fasting.”"
"2998","Musa bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, he said: Abdullah bin Farukh told us, on the authority of Umm Salamah, She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss me while he was fasting and I was fasting.” He mentioned the difference between Ash-Shabi and Zakariya, meaning Ibn Abi Zaida in it"
"2999","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Musa bin Marwan told us, saying: Abu Saeed, meaning Al-Ansari, told us, on the authority of Zakaria, saying: Saleh told me Ibn Abi Salih, who said: Muhammad Ibn Al-Ash’ath told me, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not abstain from anything.” from My presence while he was fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3000","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Ibn Abi Zaida told me, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Salih Al-Asadi, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Al-Ash'ath Ibn Qais, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not refrain from anything before me while he was fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3001","Abd al-Malik al-Raqqi ibn Abd al-Hamid, from the descendants of Maimoon ibn Mihran, informed me. He said: Ibn Hanbal told us, he said: Waki` told us, He said: Zakaria told us, on the authority of Abbas bin Dhurayh, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He, peace be upon him, does not abstain from anything before me while he is fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3002","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad reported, on the authority of Ubaidah, who said: Mutarrif told me, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, will continue fasting and kiss anywhere he wants on my face until he breaks his fast. Mention of the disagreement over Abu Ad-Duha Muslim bin Subayh and the disagreement over Al-A’mash. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3003","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel reported, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Shutair bin Shakl such-and-such, he said: On the authority of Hafsa, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss while he was fasting.”"
"3004","Muawiyah bin Salih told me, he said: Yahya bin Ma’in told me, he said: Ibn Abi Zaida told me, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Muslim, On the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss while he was fasting, but he was a slave to his father.”"
"3005","I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Our Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, and Mansour, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Shutair bin Shakl bin Humaid, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “He used to kiss while fasting.” The disagreement over Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3006","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Muslim bin Subaih, on the authority of Shutair bin Shakl, on the authority of Hafsa, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss while he was fasting.”"
"3007","Ismail bin Masoud reported, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Shutair ibn Shikal, on the authority of Umm Habibah, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss while he was fasting.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is a mistake. We do not know anyone. Shu'bah continued on what he said, on the authority of Umm Habibah, and the correct view is Shutair, on the authority of Hafsa, mentioning the disagreement over Ibrahim al-Nakha'i in this hadith."
"3008","Muhammad ibn Mansour reported that he is the permissible person from the people of Mecca. He said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss him while he was fasting, and greet people while he was fasting, and your king was his master.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3009","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Mugheerah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Alqamah and Al-Aswad told him, on the authority of Aisha, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss while he was fasting.”"
"3010","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad reported, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, and Shuraih ibn Arta’at. They mentioned that Aisha was facing the qibla for the fasting person, and she said, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss while he was fasting, and face to face.” And he was fasting, and your slaves were devoted to his Lord.” Ishaq bin Mansour reported, he said: Abd al-Rahman reported, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Alqamah and Shurayh bin A mursal attack on Aisha similar to that (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3011","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Omar bin Abi Zaida told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not abstain from my presence while he was fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3012","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abu Lahus told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He used to kiss during the month of fasting.”"
"3013","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad reported, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, and Shurayh ibn Artaat, that they mentioned the qiblah of the fasting person in the presence of Aisha, and she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss while he was fasting.” And he is fasting, and he is your master. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3014","Ishaq bin Mansour reported, saying: Abd al-Rahman told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Alqamah and Shurayh bin He comforted Aisha, and one of them said to the other: Ask her about the qiblah for a fasting person. He said: I will not perform ritual prayers with the Mother of the Believers, so Aisha said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to kiss while he was fasting, and greet him while he was fasting, and your guardian was for his Lord.” The disagreement over Mansour ibn The pilgrim (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3015","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: A group of A man called Shurayh was martyring among them, and it was narrated that Aisha said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to have sex while he was fasting.” Then a man said: I was about to hit your head with my bow. He said: O people of Nakha, tell your friend to stop his bow from me until We will go to the Mother of the Believers. When we came, they said to Alqamah: Ask her. He said: I will not commune with her today. So she heard him. She said: What is that? I said: Did you mention that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to interact with you while he was fasting?” She said: Yes, but he was your master as his owner."
"3016","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad reported, he said: Ubaidah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: Some people went out as pilgrims or builder... Some of them said: I heard the Mother of the Believers, Aisha, say: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to give communion while he was fasting.” Then Shuraih, a man from Nakha, said: I am about to hit you with this bow. So he said: O people of Nakha, pass by your friend, so that he can stop his bow until He came to the Mother of the Believers, then he mentioned a word that means it, so we brought him to the Mother of the Believers Aisha, and some of us said: This one told us about you. That you said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to commune while he was fasting.” She said: Yes, but the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, I will rule you to raise it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3017","Al-Hussein bin Harith reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: Aisha said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, would face each other while he was fasting, and kiss him while he was fasting, and your possessions would be for his Lord.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3018","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Aisha, “that The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to give people peace while he was fasting, and he used to treat his master with you. Sufyan bin Saeed disagreed with them and narrated it, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3019","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan reported, saying: Abu Al-Nadr told us, on the authority of Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to consult me while he was fasting, but he was your master for his Lord.” Mention of the disagreement over Suleiman bin Mihran Al-Amash in it"
"3020","Ali bin Khashram Al-Maruzi reported, he said: Jesus reported, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abraham, he said: Al-Aswad said: Aisha said: “He was the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he used to eat while he was fasting, except that he was your master for his Lord.”"
"3021","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan reported, he said: Al-Nadr told us, he said: Shu’bah reported, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss and greet people while he was fasting, and he was your master’s slave.”"
"3022","Tamim ibn al-Muntasir al-Wasiti reported, he said: Ishaq reported, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Aisha, “that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to give prayers while he was fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3023","Abdullah bin Muhammad, known as the weak, reported: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, And Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to kiss while he was fasting, and he would greet each other while he was fasting, but he was I have more power than you.” The disagreement over Abdullah bin Aoun was mentioned in this hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3024","Humayd ibn Masada Basri narrated on the authority of Bishr, who is Ibn al-Mufaddal al-Basri, who said: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Masruq and I went to the Mother of the Believers, and we said: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, have intercourse while fasting? She said: “He may have done so, but he has more money than you.”"
"3025","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail reported, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I entered, and Masruq was upon Aisha. So we said: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, have intercourse while fasting? She said: “He used to do that, but he had more hope than you.”"
"3026","And while Ahmad bin Mani’ read to us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ibn Aoun reported, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, he said: I said: Did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, have sexual intercourse while fasting? She said: “He might have done that, but he was more likely to be afraid of you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3027","And while Ahmad bin Mani’ read to us again, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ibn Aoun reported, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, He said: I asked Aisha: Did the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, have sexual intercourse while fasting? She said: “Yes, he was doing that, but he was afraid of you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3028","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Ismail told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad and Masruq, that they entered The Mother of the Believers. They said: Did the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, have intercourse while fasting? She said: “He might have done that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3029","Humayd ibn Masada narrated on the authority of Yazid, who was Ibn Zurai’, who said: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad and Masruq, who said: We went to Aisha and said: O Mother of the Believers, did the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, have sexual intercourse while fasting? She said: “He used to do that, but he was more in charge of his master than you.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It was narrated by al-Mughirah and Hammad, and they said on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3030","Abu Bakr bin Hafs Basri, whose name is Ismail, reported on the authority of Mu`tamir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: I asked Aisha whether the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to have sexual intercourse while fasting? She said: “Yes, but he was your master for his sake.”"
"3031","Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Durhami Basri reported, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I said to Aisha: Should a fasting person have intercourse with someone who is fasting? She said: “No.” I said: Didn’t the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, use to have sex while he was fasting? She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was your ruler for his sake.”"
"3032","Al-Harith bin Miskin I read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Qasim narrated to him, that Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Al-Zubayr narrated to him, that Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair narrated to him, that he heard Aisha, It says: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the mosque in Ramadan, and said: O Messenger of God, I was burned, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him. May God bless him and grant him peace. What is the matter with him? He said: I have harmed my family. He said: “Give alms.” He said: By God, O Prophet of God, I have nothing and I am not capable of it. He said: “Sit down.” So he sat down, while Just then, a man came driving a donkey with food on it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Where is the one who was burned just now?” So the man got up. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Give this in charity.” He said: O Messenger of God, are more worthy than us? By God, we are hungry and have nothing. He said: “Eat it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3033","Issa bin Hammad reported, he said: Al-Layth reported, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja`far bin al-Zubayr, On the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, she said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I have been burned. Then he said: I had intercourse with my wife during the day in Ramadan. He said: “Give in charity, give in charity.” He said: “I have nothing.” So he ordered him to stay, and then a vein came to him. There was food in it, so he ordered him to give it in charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3034","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abdul Wahhab reported, he said: Yahya bin Saeed reported, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, saying: Muhammad bin Jafar bin Al-Zubayr told me that Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr told him that Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, told him, She said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I was burned, so he asked him what’s wrong with him? He said: I broke my fast during Ramadan, then he sat down. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought a large measure called an arak, in which were dates. He asked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the man, and he said: Where is the burnt person? So the man got up to him and said: Give this in charity. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3035","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far bin al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah. Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have been burned. He said: “What is the matter with you?” he said. : I had intercourse with my wife during Ramadan, and a measure of food was brought to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Where “The burnt one?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3036","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Naysaburi and Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Tirmidhi reported, saying: Ayoub ibn Sulayman told us, he said: Abu Bakr told me, and he is Ibn Abi Uwais, on the authority of Suleiman, Yahya bin Saeed said: Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, that Abu Hurairah He told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered a man who broke his fast in Ramadan to make expiation by freeing a slave or fasting for two months, or Feeding sixty poor people. The man said: O Messenger of God, I cannot find it. So he was brought a handful of dates. He said: “Take this and give it in charity.” He said: Is there anyone more in need, O Messenger of God, than me? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed until his fangs showed, then he said: “Eat it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3037","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, he said: Ashhab told me, that Malik, and Al-Layth told me, that Ibn Shihab told them, on the authority of Humayd Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man broke his fast in Ramadan, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to make amends by freeing A slave, or fasting for two months, or feeding sixty needy people.” Malik said in his hadith: He said: I do not find anything, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought. He was greeted with a bunch of dates and said: “Take this and give it in charity.” He said: O Messenger of God, no one is more in need than me. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, laughed. peace be upon him until his fangs showed, then he said: “All of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3038","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Humayd bin Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, That a man had intercourse with his wife during Ramadan, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked a fatwa about that, and he said: “Can you find a slave?” He said: No, He said: “Are you able to fast for two months?” He said: No. He said: “Feed sixty poor people.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is correct, and a hadith. Ashhab attributed the hadith of Al-Layth to the hadith of Malik."
"3039","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: A man came To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I have perished. He said: “What is the matter with you?” He said: I had intercourse with my wife during the month of Ramadan. He said: “So did Can you free a slave? He said: No. He said: Can you fast for two consecutive months? He said: No. He said: Can you feed? Sixty poor people? He said: No, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought with an arab, and the arak was a huge measure. He said: Take this and give it in charity. He said: O Messenger of God, is there more need for your family than we do? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed until his fangs showed, then he said: “Feed him to your children.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3040","Muhammad bin Qudamah Al-Masisi told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Muhammad Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, a man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: The other had intercourse with his wife during Ramadan, and he said to him: “Do you find something wrong?” “You free a slave?” He said: “No.” He said: “Can you fast for two consecutive months?” He said: “No.” He said: “So you can feed sixty poor people?” He said: “No.” Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought a basket containing dates, which were ginger, and he said: “Feed this man on your behalf.” He said: Am I in need more than we are? He said: “Feed your family with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3041","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud told me, he said: Abu Al-Aswad and Ishaq bin Bakr bin Mudar told us, they said: Bakr bin Mudar told us, On the authority of Ja`far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Aarak bin Malik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him that he had intercourse with his wife during Ramadan. He said: “Do you find a slave?” He said: No. He said: He said: “Can you fast for two consecutive months?” He said: “No.” He said: “Feed sixty poor people.” He said: “I cannot find it.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave it to him. “And he ordered him to give them in charity. Then he mentioned his need to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered him to take it himself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3042","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told me, he said: Abu Muammar told me, he said: Abd al-Warith bin Saeed told us, he said: Husayn told us. The teacher, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, said: Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Awza’i told me, on the authority of Ya’ish bin al-Walid bin Hisham, that His father told him. He said: Ma’dan bin Talha told me that Abu Darda told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Q. So he broke his fast. I found a garment in his mosque, and I said: Abu Darda’ told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met and broke his fast. He said: And I poured his ablution for him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3043","Amr bin Ali reported, he said: Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith told me, he said: my father told me, he said: Hussein al-Mu’allim told me, he said: he told me Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: Al-Awza’i told me, on the authority of Ya’ish bin Al-Walid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ma’dan bin Talha, on the authority of Abu Darda’ On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “he vomited and broke his fast,” so I found two garments in the Damascus Mosque, so I mentioned that to him, and he said: He is right, I am. I poured water for him to perform his ablution. Abdul Rahman said: The correct thing is Maadan bin Abi Talha. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3044","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, saying: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to me, saying: I heard my father narrating, he said: Husayn narrated to us, he said: narrated to us Yahya bin Abi Kathir, that Abdullah bin Amr Al-Awza’i narrated to him, that Ya’ish bin Al-Walid narrated to him, that Ma’dan bin Talha He told him that Abu al-Darda’ told him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “vowed and broke his fast,” so I found two garments in the mosque of Damascus and remembered That is for him, so he said: He is right, I poured his ablution for him. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake, and this is how I found it in my book. It is Abd al-Rahman Ibn Amr al-Awza’i mentioned the disagreement over Hisham al-Dastawa’i in this hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3045","Abdah bin Abd al-Rahim al-Marwazi told me, he said: Ibn Shumayl reported, he said: Hisham al-Dastawi reported, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir. On the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ya’ish ibn Al-Walid ibn Hisham, on the authority of Ma’dan, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “qa So he broke his fast. I found a garment in the Damascus Mosque and I asked him, and he said: Yes, I poured water for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to perform his ablution. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3046","Suleiman bin Salam reported, he said: Al-Nadr reported, he said: Hisham reported, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ya’ish ibn al-Walid ibn Hisham, on the authority of Abu Ma'dan, on the authority of Abu al-Darda', that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, \vowed and broke his fast"
"3047","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham reported, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ya’ish ibn al-Walid ibn Hisham, that Ma'dan told him, that Abu Darda told him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a vomit and broke his fast. I found two garments in Damascus Mosque. I mentioned that to him and he said: I poured water for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for his ablution. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3048","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Yazid, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ya’ish bin Al-Walid, that Khalid bin Ma’dan told him, on the authority of Abu Darda’, “that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, vomited and broke his fast.” So I found two garments In the Damascus Mosque, so I mentioned that to him, and he said: I poured water for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for his ablution. Ubayd Allah bin Saeed Sarkhasi, called Abu Qudamah, reported on the authority of Muadh bin Hisham, who said: My father told me, on the authority of Yahya, he said: He told me A man, from our brothers, on the authority of Ya’ish ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Khalid ibn Ma’dan, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, and the like. Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya, he said: A man from our brothers told me, on the authority of Ya’ish Ibn Al-Walid, that Ibn Ma’dan told him something similar to the hadith of Abraham (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3049","Ahmad bin Fadalah bin Ibrahim Al-Nasa’i told me, he said: Abd al-Razzaq reported, he said: Mu’mar reported, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ya’ish, on the authority of Khaled bin Maadan, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, vomited and broke his fast. Water was brought and he performed ablution.”"
"3050","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Issa bin Yunus reported, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “If a fasting person vomits, he does not have to break his fast, and if he vomits, he must make up for it.” Ataa’s waqfah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3051","Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated, saying: Hibban narrated to us, saying: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah narrated to me, on the authority of my father Hurairah said: “Whoever vomits while fasting, let him break his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3052","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Ulayya, the judge of Damascus, informed me. He said: Abu Amir told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Thawban, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper and the one who uses the cup break his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3053","Ahmad bin Fadalah bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Makhoul told me, that An old man from the neighborhood told him that Thawban told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper and the one who uses the cup break his fast.”"
"3054","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Khalid told us, saying: Ibn Jurayj told us, saying: Makhoul told me, on the authority of a living sheikh, Musaddiq, on the authority of Thawban, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper and the one having the procedure break his fast,” from the Sheikh. Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, on the authority of Marwan, who is the son of Muhammad al-Tatri, he said: Al-Haytham bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Harith, On the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abu Asma, on the authority of Thawban and something similar, followed by Rashid bin Daoud. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3055","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Marwan told us, he said: Yahya bin Hamza told us, he said: Rashid bin Daoud told me, he said: Abu Asma al-Rahbi told me, on the authority of Thawban, who said: I walked with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the eighteenth of Ramadan, which had passed. A man was performing cupping, and he said: “The cupper and the one being cupped broke his fast.” Mention of the disagreement over Abu Qilaba Abdullah bin Zaid Al-Jarmi"
"3056","Ismail bin Masoud reported, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, that Abu Asma Al-Rahbi narrated to him, that Thawban narrated to him, he said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was walking in Al-Baqi’ in Ramadan, when a man He performs cupping, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper and the one being cupped break his fast.” Mansour bin Zazan disagreed with him, and he narrated it, on the authority of Abu Qalabah On the authority of Abu Al-Ash'ath, on the authority of Shaddad"
"3057","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad reported, saying: Khidr bin Muhammad told us, saying: Hushaym reported, saying: Mansour reported, on the authority of Abu Qalaba. And Anba Khalid reported, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: I was walking with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year of the conquest of He went to Mecca on the eighteenth or nineteenth of Ramadan, and he passed by a man who was using cupping, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Break your fast.” The cupper and the stoned “the disagreement over Ayoub” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3058","Ismail reported, saying: Asim bin Hilal told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Asma, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, he said: While The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was holding my hand along the way for eighteen nights that passed during Ramadan, when he saw a man cupping, and he said: The cupper and the one being cupped broke his fast.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abbad bin Mansour combined the two hadiths, saying: On the authority of Abu Asma’, on the authority of Thawban, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws"
"3059","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam al-Tarsusi told me, he said: Rayhan bin Saeed told us, he said: Abbad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Abu Asma al-Rahbi, on the authority of Thawban, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a man who was cupping during Ramadan, and he said: “ “The cupper and the one being cupped broke his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3060","Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad told me, he said: Rayhan bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abbad, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, Shaddad bin Aws told him that while he was walking with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Medina during Ramadan, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was holding Shaddad’s hand when he came upon a man who was cupping, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper and the one being cupped have broken the fast,” he said. Abu Abd al-Rahman: Abbad bin Mansour is not an authority in the hadith, and it was said: Rayhan is not accustomed to hearing from him, and Jarir disagreed with him. So he sent him. Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id reported, saying: I heard Wahb ibn Jarir saying: My father said: I showed Ayyub a letter from Abu Qilaba, and lo, in it was On the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, and Thawban this hadith, he said: I showed it to him and he recognized it. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Hammad bin Zayd followed him. On his message, on the authority of Shaddad, and he is the most knowledgeable of people about Ayoub. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3061","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, he referred it to Shaddad bin Aws, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “The cupper and the one being cupped break his fast.” Sufyan agreed to send him."
"3062","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ibn Abi Omar told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, he said: I passed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man in Al-Baqi’ while he was cupping on the seventeenth day of Ramadan, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The cupper and the one being cupped broke his fast.” It was narrated by Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abi Qalabah, contrary to Ayyub’s narration. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3063","Ali bin Al-Mundhir, a Shiite Kufi, reported, saying: Ibn Fudayl told us, saying: Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, on the authority of Abi Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Abi Asma’, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by on the eighteenth of Ramadan. Then he saw a man performing cupping, and he said: “The cupper and the one being cupped have broken their fast.” Abu Ghaffar followed him."
"3064","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna narrated, saying: Sahl bin Yusuf narrated to us, saying: Abu Ghaffar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Asma’, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was holding my hand for the eighteen days that had passed during Ramadan, when he turned to He saw a man performing cupping, so he said: “The cupper and the one being cupped broke his fast.” The disagreement over Asim bin Suleiman (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3065","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya and Ahmad bin Suleiman Al-Rahwi reported, saying: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Asim reported, On the authority of Abdullah ibn Zayd, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath al-San’ani, on the authority of Abu Asma al-Rahbi, on the authority of Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: I passed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. On the eighteenth day of Ramadan, he saw a man using cupping, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper broke his fast.” The “al-mahjum” is followed by an additional letter (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3066","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad reported, saying: Yahya bin Ya’la bin al-Harith al-Muharbi told us, saying: Zaida told us, on the authority of Asim. Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Asma Al-Rahbi, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, who said: While I was walking with the Prophet, he prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, when he passed by a man who was performing cupping during Ramadan, and he said: “The cupper and the one being cupped have broken their fast.” Hisham and Shu’bah disagreed with them. And Sufyan bin Habib (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3067","Abdullah bin Al-Sabbah bin Abdullah Al-Attar Al-Basri reported, saying: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, On the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath al-San’ani, on the authority of Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was taking my hand in the morning The eighteen days of Ramadan had passed, when the time of Ramadan came and a man was performing cupping, and he said: “The cupper and the one being cupped have broken his fast.”"
"3068","Abdah bin Abd al-Rahim al-Marwazi told me, he said: Ibn Shumayl reported, he said: Shu’bah reported, on the authority of Asim, and Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalaba. On the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Shaddad ibn Aws, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper and the one being operated on break the fast.”"
"3069","Al-Hasan bin Qazah Basri narrated, saying: Sufyan bin Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Asim and Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man performing cupping during Ramadan, and he said: “The cupper and the one being cupped broke his fast.” He mentioned The disagreement over Khalid bin Mahran regarding which shoes to wear."
"3070","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, He was holding the hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the time of the conquest, and he passed by a man who was performing cupping in Ramadan, and he said: “The cupper and the one being treated have broken their fast.” \""
3071"""
"3071","'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Yazid (ibn Zuray') narrated to us, saying: Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a man who was cupping (hijamah) on the eighteenth day of Ramadan, and he said: 'The cupper and the one being cupped have broken their fast.'"""
"3072","Abu Asim reported, he said: Abd al-Razzaq reported, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdullah, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Asma, on the authority of Shaddad Ibn Aws, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper and the one being cupped break his fast.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ismail is a man. It is unknown and we do not know it. The correct hadith from Khalid is what we mentioned above, even though Qatada had narrated it as well."
"3073","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Asmaa, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out on the eighteenth of Ramadan and saw a man using cupping. He said: “The cupper and the one being cupped broke his fast.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Qatada, whom we do not know, heard something from Abu Qilabah, and it was narrated by Yazid ibn Harun, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Bilal (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3074","Zakaria ibn Yahya told me, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Qatada about a month, On the authority of Bilal, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The cupper and the one being performed have broken their fast.” Hammam disagreed with them, and he narrated it on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of a month, About Thawban (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3075","Muhammad bin Muammar Basri reported, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of a month, on the authority of Thawban, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The cupper and the one being cupped broke his fast.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Sa’id bin Abi Arouba entered between a month and two days. Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanam (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3076","Ismail bin Masoud reported, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanam, on the authority of Thawban, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper and the person having the procedure have broken their fast.” Bukayr bin Abi Al-Sumait disagreed with them and narrated it, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Maadan, on the authority of Thuban"
"3077","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id reported, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Bukayr ibn Abi al-Sumait told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ma’dan. Ibn Abi Talha, on the authority of Thawban, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper and the one being cupped break his fast,” Abu Abd al-Rahman said. Al-Layth bin Saad disagreed with them, and he narrated it, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Thawban."
"3078","Qutaybah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Thawban, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The cupper and the person undergoing the procedure broke their fast.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I did not know that anyone followed al-Layth or Bukair ibn Abi al-Sumait, according to their narrations. And God knows best. It was narrated by Omar bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3079","Al-Hasan bin Ahmad reported, saying: Shath bin Fayyad Basri narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Ibrahim Basri, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The cupper and the one being cupped break his fast.” Abu Al-Ala’ stopped him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3080","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Suraij told us, he said: Muhammad bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, On the authority of Ali, he said: “The cupper and the one being cupped broke his fast.” The disagreement over Saeed bin Abi Arouba was mentioned in this hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3081","Zakaria bin Yahya Sijistani told me, he said: Amr bin Issa told us, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, said: “The cupper and the one being cupped break his fast.”"
"3082","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Minhal told us, he said: Ibn Zurayi told us, he said: Ibn Abi Arouba told us, On the authority of Matar, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The cupper and the one having the procedure break his fast.” Ash’ath ibn Abd disagreed with him. The king narrated it, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, and no one we knew of followed him based on his narration. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3083","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated, saying: Sulaym ibn Akhdar narrated, saying: Ash’ath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Usama ibn Zayd, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He broke the fast, meaning the cupper and the one having the procedure.”"
"3084","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Abu Dawud told me, saying: Sulayman bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: A group of people testified with me. Among the people of Basra was Al-Hasan, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man using cupping while he was fasting. He said: “The cupper and the one being cupped have broken their fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3085","Yahya bin Musa and Ahmad bin Harb reported, and the word for it, he said: Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: A group of people testified with me. The people of Basra included Al-Hasan bin Abi Al-Hasan, on the authority of Maqil bin Sinan Al-Ashja’i, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by me. I was performing cupping on the eighteenth of Ramadan, and he said: “The cupper and the one being cupped have broken their fast.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib had He mixed up, and we do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from him except these two, despite their disagreement about it. And God knows best, this hadith was narrated by Abu Free, about Al-Hasan, and there was disagreement over him about it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3086","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Hurra told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Both the cupper and the one having the procedure done break the fast.” I said: From whom? He said: On the authority of more than one of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Bishr ibn al-Sirri and Abu Qatn gave him endowments. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3087","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Bishr bin Al-Sari told us, he said: Abu Hurrah told us, he said: Matar Al-Warraq ordered me to ask Al-Hasan about the one who narrated this hadith: “The cupper and the one being cupped break his fast.” So I asked him, and he said: On the authority of more than one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3088","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Suraij told us, he said: Abu Qatn told us, on the authority of Abu Hurra, he said: I said to Al-Hasan: Your statement: “The cupper and the one being cupped broke his fast.” From whom? He said: On the authority of more than one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, followed by Sulayman al-Taymi. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3089","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Al-Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of more than one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon them. They said: “The cupper and the one being cupped broke his fast.” The disagreement over Yunus bin Ubaid was mentioned regarding it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3090","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal disagreed with “the cupper and the one being cupped.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3091","Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala reported, saying: Al-Mu`tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abi Amr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The cupper and the one having the procedure break his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3092","Ahmad bin Fadalah Al-Nasa’i reported, he said: Abu Asim reported, he said: Ibn Jurayj reported, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, a client of Bani Amer, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a man performing cupping during Ramadan on the morning of eighteen, and he said: “The cupper broke his fast.” “And the stoned one.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith, and I think that Ibn Jurayj did not hear it from Safwan. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3093","Ayoub bin Muhammad Al-Wazzan told me, he said: Muammar bin Sulayman told us, he said: Abdullah bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper and the one having the procedure break his fast.” Ibrahim stopped him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3094","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah Nisaburi Murji reported, saying: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman Harawi told me. Murji’, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: “The cupper and the one having the procedure break his fast.”"
"3095","Muhammad bin Hatim reported, he said: Hibban reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Muammar. And Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Issa told us, he said: Ibn Al-Mubarak informed, he said: Muammar informed, on the authority of Khallad, on the authority of a brother Ibn Thawr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: It is said: “The cupper and the one being cupped break his fast,” but as for me, if I had cupped, I would not have minded. Abu Hurairah says: This wording is from Zakaria, who mentioned the disagreement over Ata’ bin Abi Rabah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3096","Hafs bin Omar Al-Razi reported, he said: Abu Ahmad reported, on the authority of Rabah bin Abi Marouf, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper and the one having the procedure break his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3097","Muhammad bin Idris reported to Abu Hatim al-Razi, saying: Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper and the one having the procedure break his fast.” Dawoud bin Abdul Rahman followed him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3098","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Abdul Ala told us, he said: Dawud bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, “The cupper and the one being cupped break his fast.” Abd al-Razzaq and al-Nadr bin Shammil"
"3099","Suleiman bin Salam Al-Balkhi reported, he said: Al-Nadr reported, he said: Ibn Jurayj reported, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The hajm broke the fast.” “And the one who uses cupping,” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: “Ata’, which he did not hear from Abu Hurairah.”"
"3100","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The cupper and the one who uses the cup break his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3101","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and he did not hear it from him. He said: The cupper and the one being examined broke his fast.” Ibn Abi Husayn disagreed with him, and he narrated it, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah"
"3102","Al-Hasan bin Ishaq Maruzi reported, saying: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Raqqashi told us, saying: Wahib told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hussein, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: “The cupper and the one being cupped break his fast.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The correct thing is Hajjaj’s narration, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, because Amr Ibn Dinar followed him on that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3103","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Hajjaj, he said: Shu’bah told me, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of a man, on the authority of my father Hurairah, he said: “The cupper and the one being cupped broke his fast.” He mentioned the disagreement over Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulaiman regarding it."
"3104","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Yazid, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman reported, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: “The cupper and the one being cupped break his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3105","Muhammad bin Hatim reported, he said: Hibban reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said : “The cupper and the one being cupped broke his fast.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Khalid bin Abdullah disagreed with them and made it from the saying “‘taa’.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3106","Saeed bin Yaqoub Al-Talqani reported, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “ “The cupper and the one being cupped broke his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3107","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Khalaf bin Salem told us, he said: Abu Al-Nadr told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ataa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper and the one having the procedure break his fast.” Al-Hasan bin Musa stopped him."
"3108","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, he said Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Iyad bin Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “Iftar “The cupper and the one being cupped.” Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad agreed with him."
"3109","Abu Bakr bin Ali reported, saying: Abbas al-Narsi told us, saying: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ata’, He said: Aisha used to say: “The cupper and the one being cupped broke the fast.” Abdullah bin Lahi’ah bin Uqba disagreed with them and narrated it, on the authority of Ata’. On the authority of Abu al-Darda’, Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated it on his authority, Fitr ibn Khalifa disagreed with them, if it was a short story that had been preserved on his authority, so he narrated it on the authority of Ataa, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3110","Uqba bin Qubaisa bin Uqba reported, he said: My father told me, he said: Fitr told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet said, May God bless him and grant him peace: “The cupper and the one being cupped break his fast.” Muhammad ibn Yusuf disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3111","Ahmad bin Al-Azhar told us about Al-Naysaburi, he said: Muhammad bin Yusuf told us, he said: Fitr told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: We had heard that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The cupper and the one who uses the cup break his fast.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Layth bin Abi Sulaym does not use his hadith as evidence. The opposite of this was narrated on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3112","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abu Malik Bishr bin Al-Hasan, trustworthy, brother of Hussein bin Hassan, told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us On the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used the beard of a camel while he was fasting and in Muharram,” and it was narrated on the authority of Ibn Abbas said that he did not see any harm in cupping for a fasting person. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3113","Muhammad bin Hatim reported, he said: Hibban reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Yahya, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that “he did not There is no harm in cupping for the fasting person.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Dahhak did not hear from Ibn Abbas, and the hadith of Ibn Hasan is with me. And God knows best, they are an illusion, and perhaps he wanted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to “marry while in ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3114","Ahmad bin Nasr Al-Naysaburi reported, saying: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger May God bless him and grant him peace. “He married Maimuna while he was in Ihram.” Sent by Sufyan bin Habib"
"3115","Humayd bin Masada Al-Basri reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “married while he was in ihram.” “Mentioning the disagreement over Al-Awza’i regarding it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3116","Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Sulayman al-Dimashqi told me, he said: Yazid told us, and he is al-Dimashqi, he said: Al-Walid told us, Abu Amr said. Al-Awza’i: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, he said: Ata’ told me, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Maimunah while he was \Forbidden\"""""
"3117","Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq Dimashqi told me, he said: Abu Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “married Maimuna while he was in a state of ihram.” Ibn Ishaq followed him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3118","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Ibn Abi Zaida, he said: Ibn Ishaq reported, on the authority of Aban bin Salih, on the authority of Mujahid, and Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “married Maimuna while he was in a state of ihram,” and it is well-known on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was cupped while in ihram and mentioned the disagreement over Laith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3119","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawoos, and Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he was treated with cupping while he was in ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3120","Muhammad bin Mansour Makki reported on the authority of Sufyan. Amr told us: I heard Ata’. He said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cupped his hands.” “peace and blessings of God be upon him while he was in ihram.” Then he later said: Tawus told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cupped while he was in ihram. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3121","Muhammad bin Maadan bin Issa reported, saying: Al-Hasan bin Ayan reported, saying: Maqil told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “He cupped Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in Ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3122","Issa bin Hammad reported, he said: Al-Layth reported, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He was cupped while he was in ihram.” Mention of the difference between those reporting the news of Abu Musa Abdullah bin Qais regarding cupping for the fasting person (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3123","Al-Hasan bin Ishaq reported, saying: Ruh bin Ubadah told us, saying: Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Bakr bin Abd. Allah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, said: I entered upon Abu Musa at night, and he was having cupping, so I said: Wasn’t this during the day? He said: My blood was shed while I was fasting, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The cupper and the one being cupped break his fast,” Abu Abd said. Al-Rahman: This is a mistake, and Hafs stopped it. Hussein bin Mansour reported, he said: Hafs told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, On the authority of Abu Musa, he said. . . And he did not raise it"
"3124","Muhammad ibn Bashar reported, he said: Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of Abu Musa, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The cupper and the one having the procedure break his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3125","Ahmad Ibn Al-Azhar reported, saying: Sa’id Ibn Amir told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of a friend of his, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Buraidah, who said: He entered upon One night, Abu Musa was performing cupping, and it was said to him: If this had been daytime, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper broke the fast.” “And the one who is stoned.”"
"3126","Hussein bin Mansour Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Hafs told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Orouba told us, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, he said: I entered upon Abu Musa while he was cupping at night, so I said: Was this during the day? He said: You command me to shed my blood while I am fasting, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The cupper and the one being operated on break the fast.” He mentioned The disagreement over Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani regarding it"
"3127","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, said: I entered Abu Musa while he was cupping at night, so I said: Wasn’t this during the day? He said: “Do you order me to shed my blood while I am fasting?” Humaid al-Tawil disagreed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3128","Humayd ibn Masada narrated, saying: Bishr narrated to us, saying: Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, that he entered upon Abu Musa He was the prince of Basra at sunset, and he found him eating dates and dates. He said: I had cupping. He said: Didn’t you have cupping during the day? He said: “You command me to shed my blood while I am fasting?” And he is fasting"
"3129","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala reported, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Zayd, on the authority of Ikrimah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used cupping while fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3130","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Surayj told us, he said: Abdullah bin Raja told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used cupping in a place where it was said: A camel may drink water while he was fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3131","Bishr ibn Hilal reported, he said: Abd al-Warith told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He was cupped while fasting."
"3132","Muhammad bin Muammar reported, saying: Hibban told us, saying: Wahib told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He was cupped while fasting. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3133","Qattan bin Ibrahim Al-Naysaburi informed us, saying: Al-Hussein bin Al-Walid Al-Naysaburi narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cupped while he was in the state of Ihram, and he cupped while fasting.”"
"3134","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Al-Qawariri told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He was cupped while fasting.”"
"3135","Muhammad ibn Hatim reported, he said: Hibban reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: He was cupped while fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
